1mNAME0m
     nvme-sndk-vs-temperature-stats - Display temperature-related statistics

1mSYNOPSIS0m
     4mnvme24m [<global-options>] 4msndk24m 4mvs-temperature-stats24m <device>

1mDESCRIPTION0m
     For the NVMe device given, displays temperature statistics.

     The <device> parameter is mandatory NVMe character device (ex: /dev/nvme0).

     This  will  only  work on Sandisk devices supporting this feature. Results for any other device
     are undefined.

     Expected status and description :- allbox tab(:); ltB ltB.  T{ Statistic T}:T{  Description  T}
     lt lt lt lt lt lt lt lt lt lt lt lt lt lt lt lt lt lt lt lt lt lt lt lt.  T{

     The current composite temperature T}:T{

     device temperature T} T{

     Warning Composite TEMPerature threshold T}:T{

     temp of overheating T} T{

     Critical Composite TEMPerature threshold T}:T{

     temp of critical overheating T} T{

     Device Initiated Thermal Throttling support status T}:T{

     0 = unsupported, 1 = supported T} T{

     Host Controlled Thermal Management support T}:T{

     0 = unsupported, 1 = supported T} T{

     Thermal Management Temperature 1 (Light throttle) T}:T{

     temp to start light throttle T} T{

     Thermal Management Temperature 1 Transition Counter T}:T{

     # times switched into light throttle T} T{

     Thermal Management Temperature 1 Total Time T}:T{

     # seconds spent in light throttle T} T{

     Thermal Management Temperature 2 (Heavy throttle) T}:T{

     temp to start heavy throttle T} T{

     Thermal Management Temperature 2 Transition Counter T}:T{

     # times switched into heavy throttle T} T{

     Thermal Management Temperature 2 Total Time T}:T{

     # seconds spent in heavy throttle T} T{

     Thermal Shutdown Threshold T}:T{

     temp of device shutdown T}


     On success it returns 0, error code otherwise.

1mOPTIONS0m
1mGLOBAL OPTIONS0m
     The  following options are defined at the top-level nvme command and are available to this sub‐
     command:

     --dry-run
         Print the command that would be executed, but do not actually execute it.

     --no-ioctl-probing
         Disable probing for 64-bit IOCTL support.

     --no-retries
         Disable retry logic on transient errors.

     -o <fmt>, --output-format=<fmt>
         Set the reporting format to 4mnormal24m, 4mtabular,24m 4m'json24m, or 4mbinary24m. Only one output  format  may
         be used at a time.

     --output-format-version=<version>
         Select the output format version. Version 4m124m uses the original field naming, while version 4m20m
         (default)  provides more consistent and script-friendly field names. Other versions are re‐
         jected.

     --quiet
         Suppress informational messages. Errors are still reported, and --quiet cancels any  --ver‐
         bose for the library log level.

     --set-options=<key=value>[,<key=value>...]
         Set  libnvme library options for this invocation. Supported keys are 4mforce-4k24m, 4mmi-probe-en‐0m
         4mabled24m, 4mtest-base-dir24m and 4mtest-sysfs-dir24m.

     --timeout=<ms>
         Set the timeout for the command in milliseconds.  4minfinite24m or 4m-124m waits without a time limit
         (0xffffffff).

     -v, --verbose
         Increase the level of detail in the output. May be specified multiple times to further  in‐
         crease verbosity.

     These options can also be set as machine-wide defaults in nvme-cli.conf(5). A command-line flag
     always overrides the file.

1mEXAMPLES0m
     •   Displays the temperature stats for the device:

             # nvme sndk vs-temperature-stats /dev/nvme0

